  "summary_student": "The lunar habitat plan uses air with at least 30% oxygen at a pressure of 10.2 psi or less. Among the NASA tests that used that much oxygen, 8 of 32 burning-droplet tests and 66 of 468 gas-flame tests also matched the low pressure. No test of burning solid materials, the main fire risk inside a habitat, used that much oxygen, so for solids there is no data.",
  "summary_professional": "Applying the lunar_base atmosphere (O2 at least 30% O2, pressure at most 10.2 psi), 500 PSI tests reached the oxygen threshold: 32 droplet tests (FLEX PSI-69, FLEX-2 PSI-68), of which 8 also ran at or below 10.2 psi and 0 lack a pressure value; and 468 gas-flame tests (Flame Design PSI-10, CFI-G PSI-159, BRE PSI-20), of which 66 also met the pressure limit and 16 report no pressure (the BRE test days). Solid-fuel and smoke tests do not appear in the values: no solid test with an oxygen value reached the threshold and the remaining solid and smoke rows give no oxygen, which is no data, not zero.",
